 "label": "In Arabic, the no-space continuation piece 'ور' fires when it directly follows the token ' أم' (أمور/أمورهم), while the same 'ور' after any other prefix (نور, مرور, أجور, even الأمور via ' الأم') stays near floor, so for 'ور' the unit reads the ' أم'+'ور' bigram rather than the piece; the standalone piece 'م' (أمم as ' أم'+'م', corpus لِيُؤْمِنُوا) also fires with or without ' أم' before it, and ' أم' as a standalone word before a space-initial token is not claimed.",
